4587254	2025-12-13 14:30:00	<div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div tabindex="-1"><div><div dir="ltr"><div><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Australian music company Bird’s Robe will wrap up their 15th anniversary celebrations in Melbourne with a massive show at Max Watts </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><span tabindex="0"><span><span><span><span><span><span>on Saturday</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> <span><span><span><span><span tabindex="0"><span><span><span><span><span><span>13 December</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TYiz27KeuWA" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>WATCH THE TOUR ANNOUNCE TRAILER</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></a></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Headlining the last of three Melbourne events are </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>post-rock legends sleepmakeswaves</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, playing their </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>first shows of 2025</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, alongside </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>American alternative rock icons …And You Will Know Us By The Trail of Dead</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, returning to Australia for the </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>first time in over a decade</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>The day kicks off at 2.30pm</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span> and showcases a dynamic lineup from the Bird’s Robe family. Highlights include Melbourne rock trailblazers Closure in Moscow, a prog feast from Toehider &amp; Anubis, pummelling post-metal from Myriad Drone &amp; Echotide, and rare live appearances from Kodiak Empire &amp; the theremin-fuelled psych explorations of Sydney’s Svntax Error.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>The show will also feature artist signings, merch giveaways and a competitive table tennis competition.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Alex Wilson from sleepmakeswaves said of Bird’s Robe/Mike Solo:</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span>“Bird’s Robe &amp; Mike Solo…people will have lots of things to say about. He is just as much responsible as any member of the band for any of the success that sleepmakeswaves is perceived as having.”</span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>The celebration coincides with the release of the </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>Bird’s Robe documentary series</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, which premiered its first episode in July. New episodes drop </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>fortnightly from July through December.</strong></span></span></span></span></b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iADZG5ZvYy8" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Watch Episode 1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></a></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Bird’s Robe has long been a launchpad for some of Australia’s most acclaimed post-rock and progressive artists, including </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>sleepmakeswaves, We Lost The Sea, Closure in Moscow, Toehider, Meniscus, The Crooked Fiddle Band, Troldhaugen</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, and </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>Solkyri</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, among others.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Across its 15-year journey, the label has promoted more than </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>1,500 live shows</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span> and released over </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>200 records</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, including </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>five ARIA-nominated albums</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span> and </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>seven #1 releases on the Australian Independent Charts</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>. Its catalogue has collectively amassed </span></span></span></span><b><span><span><span><span><strong>over 50 million streams</strong></span></span></span></span></b><span><span><span><span>, underscoring the label’s impact both locally and internationally.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Director Mike Solo says:</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span>Ten years ago, </span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><i><span tabindex="0"><span><span><span><span><span><span>on Saturday</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><i> </i></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><i><span tabindex="0"><span><span><span><span><span><span>5 December</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span> in 2015, a bunch of bands playing post-rock, prog, metal and alternative rock got together at Manning Bar in Sydney, Australia to celebrate the 5<sup>th</sup> anniversary of Bird’s Robe Records.&nbsp; It was awesome.</span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span>Since then, we’ve crossed the globe many more times, survived a global pandemic and come out the other side with even more talent to showcase from our little niche.&nbsp; So please join us to relive the memories, create new ones &amp; celebrate an epic ride of prog, post rock, and otherwise innovative music with our friends &amp; family.</span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span>If you’ve never had the chance to see some of these bands, we hope our efforts to bring them all together in the one place make for a worthy day/night of entertainment.</span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><i><span><span><span><span>Enjoy!</span></span></span></span></i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Details and tickets from </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><a href="https://www.birdsrobe.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>www.<wbr>birdsrobe.<wbr>com</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></a></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>	1035959424	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1035959424?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:21:18	2025-10-24 12:36:17	{"...And You Will Know Us By The Trail Of Dead",sleepmakeswaves}	5771	t
4587255	2025-11-29 17:00:00	<p dir="ltr">The second line-up announcement for Tāmaki Makaurau&rsquo;s favourite street festival has just dropped, and it&rsquo;s nothing short of flipping brilliant. Saturday 29 November across Karangahape Road, there&rsquo;s only one place you should be.&nbsp;</p><p dir="ltr">Just announced as joining dozens of mind-boggling acts at&nbsp;The Others Way&nbsp;this year is<br>none other than <strong>Connan Mockasin</strong>, making his grand return to Auckland in band format for the first time in 6 years. Also appearing amongst the astounding new array of acts are Brooklyn&rsquo;s Emily Sprague-fronted band <strong>Florist</strong> (appearing as a duo); truly iconic <strong>Dead Moon</strong> founder and Portland rock&rsquo;n&rsquo;roll stalwart <strong>Toody Cole &amp; Her Band</strong>; London club queen and &ldquo;Goddess of Rhythm&rdquo; <strong>Karen Nyame KG</strong>; Melbourne folk &amp; trip-hop favourite <strong>Georgia Knight</strong>; sought after Pōneke rapper and singer-songwriter <strong>Mā; Cory Champion</strong>&rsquo;s boundary-pushing jazz outfit <strong>Clear Path Ensemble</strong>; Aotearoa Music Award-winner for Best Alternative Artist <strong>Jim Nothing</strong>; enigmatic rapper <strong>jackaltheblackal</strong>, Ōtepoti&rsquo;s big guitar sound darlings <strong>Pearly*</strong>, and the one-two collaborative punch of local rap hero <strong>Brandn Shiraz</strong> with sought after producer <strong>Caru</strong>. <br><br>In recent years, the all-ages stage at The Others Way has been one of the most vibrant places to catch the next-big-things, and this year is no exception. Down with the kids this year are Pōneke guitar slingers <strong>Dropper</strong> featuring Jude Savage (ex-Bleeding Star), Tāmaki based musician, interdisciplinary artist, and extraterrestrial witch <strong>VIDA</strong>, alternative rock band and &ldquo;clowns with hand grenades&rdquo; <strong>Capricore</strong>, &ldquo;heavy psych drifters&rdquo; <strong>Crying Ivy</strong>, and riot grrrl faves <strong>Lipstick Cherry</strong>. <br><br>The Pitt St Methodist Church stage will be a secondary all-ages space, and includes performances from <strong>Tiny Ruins (duo), Shannon Lay (US), </strong>and<strong> Holly Arrowsmith</strong>. A full stage schedule and All Ages final details will be announced in November.&nbsp;</p><p dir="ltr" style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>&ldquo;The festival where everything is awesome&rdquo; - Chris Schulz, Boiler Room&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p dir="ltr">These phenomenal new names join a truly scorching roster of previously announced acts, including the world dominating majesty of <strong>Sharon Van Etten &amp; The Attachment Theory</strong> (US), set to headline our brand new main stage.<br><br>Also on the menu, Aotearoa&rsquo;s fabled masters of big noise <strong>High Dependency Unit</strong>, back to saturate your ears for their first live shows since 2017; Canadian &ldquo;sonic nonconformist&rdquo; <strong>Saya Gray</strong> is headed our way for her debut NZ show; <strong>The Phoenix Foundation</strong> performing their recently reissued cult classic <em>Pegasus</em> in full; and Zambia&rsquo;s &ldquo;Zamrock&rdquo; legends <strong>W.I.T.C.H.</strong> are intending to cause havoc, Others Way style. All this and a heck of a lot more.</p><p>And, as a reminder, for the first time ever <strong>we&rsquo;re closing down KARANGAHAPE ROAD!</strong> Expect the whole dang block between Queen Street and Pitt Street to transform into the party of your dreams, with our main stage landing right near the Rainbow crossing.</p><p>You heard it here, folks. We&rsquo;re shutting down the street, throwing K Road the biggest party you&rsquo;ve ever seen, and bringing you the wildest line-up in the festival&rsquo;s history. You don&rsquo;t wanna miss it.<br><br><strong>PLEASE NOTE:&nbsp;</strong><br><strong>THIS IS AN ALL AGES EVENT, BUT ALL AGES TICKETS DO NOT GRANT ACCESS TO ALL ZONES, ONLY TO DEDICATED ALL AGES STAGES (FLYING OUT BASEMENT + PITT ST METHODIST CHURCH)</strong><br><br><strong>UNDER 15s MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY A PARENT OR LEGAL GUARDIAN</strong></p>	1036667369	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1036667369?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:21:20	2025-10-24 12:36:17	{"Anthonie Tonnon",BBYFACEKILLA,Capricore,"Dead Moon","High Dependency Unit","Connan Mockasin",C.O.F.F.I.N,FLORIST,"Elliot & Vincent",Hina,RNZŌ,"Romi Wrights & The Commotions","Shannon Lay","Geneva AM","Sharon Van Etten & the Attachment Theory","Swizel Jager","The Phoenix Foundation","The Bats","Tiny Ruins","Toody Cole",W.I.T.C.H.,droppER,"Christoph El Truento","Holly Arrowsmith","Brandn Shiraz","Jim Nothing",Sampology,"Karen Nyame KG","Saya Gray","clear path ensemble",Womb,"Jamaica Moana",ARAHI,"Isla Noon","Mazbou Q",jackaltheblackal}	6314	t
