4588551	2025-11-29 17:00:00	<p dir="ltr">The second line-up announcement for Tāmaki Makaurau&rsquo;s favourite street festival has just dropped, and it&rsquo;s nothing short of flipping brilliant. Saturday 29 November across Karangahape Road, there&rsquo;s only one place you should be.&nbsp;</p><p dir="ltr">Just announced as joining dozens of mind-boggling acts at&nbsp;The Others Way&nbsp;this year is<br>none other than <strong>Connan Mockasin</strong>, making his grand return to Auckland in band format for the first time in 6 years. Also appearing amongst the astounding new array of acts are Brooklyn&rsquo;s Emily Sprague-fronted band <strong>Florist</strong> (appearing as a duo); truly iconic <strong>Dead Moon</strong> founder and Portland rock&rsquo;n&rsquo;roll stalwart <strong>Toody Cole &amp; Her Band</strong>; London club queen and &ldquo;Goddess of Rhythm&rdquo; <strong>Karen Nyame KG</strong>; Melbourne folk &amp; trip-hop favourite <strong>Georgia Knight</strong>; sought after Pōneke rapper and singer-songwriter <strong>Mā; Cory Champion</strong>&rsquo;s boundary-pushing jazz outfit <strong>Clear Path Ensemble</strong>; Aotearoa Music Award-winner for Best Alternative Artist <strong>Jim Nothing</strong>; enigmatic rapper <strong>jackaltheblackal</strong>, Ōtepoti&rsquo;s big guitar sound darlings <strong>Pearly*</strong>, and the one-two collaborative punch of local rap hero <strong>Brandn Shiraz</strong> with sought after producer <strong>Caru</strong>. <br><br>In recent years, the all-ages stage at The Others Way has been one of the most vibrant places to catch the next-big-things, and this year is no exception. Down with the kids this year are Pōneke guitar slingers <strong>Dropper</strong> featuring Jude Savage (ex-Bleeding Star), Tāmaki based musician, interdisciplinary artist, and extraterrestrial witch <strong>VIDA</strong>, alternative rock band and &ldquo;clowns with hand grenades&rdquo; <strong>Capricore</strong>, &ldquo;heavy psych drifters&rdquo; <strong>Crying Ivy</strong>, and riot grrrl faves <strong>Lipstick Cherry</strong>. <br><br>The Pitt St Methodist Church stage will be a secondary all-ages space, and includes performances from <strong>Tiny Ruins (duo), Shannon Lay (US), </strong>and<strong> Holly Arrowsmith</strong>. A full stage schedule and All Ages final details will be announced in November.&nbsp;</p><p dir="ltr" style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>&ldquo;The festival where everything is awesome&rdquo; - Chris Schulz, Boiler Room&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p dir="ltr">These phenomenal new names join a truly scorching roster of previously announced acts, including the world dominating majesty of <strong>Sharon Van Etten &amp; The Attachment Theory</strong> (US), set to headline our brand new main stage.<br><br>Also on the menu, Aotearoa&rsquo;s fabled masters of big noise <strong>High Dependency Unit</strong>, back to saturate your ears for their first live shows since 2017; Canadian &ldquo;sonic nonconformist&rdquo; <strong>Saya Gray</strong> is headed our way for her debut NZ show; <strong>The Phoenix Foundation</strong> performing their recently reissued cult classic <em>Pegasus</em> in full; and Zambia&rsquo;s &ldquo;Zamrock&rdquo; legends <strong>W.I.T.C.H.</strong> are intending to cause havoc, Others Way style. All this and a heck of a lot more.</p><p>And, as a reminder, for the first time ever <strong>we&rsquo;re closing down KARANGAHAPE ROAD!</strong> Expect the whole dang block between Queen Street and Pitt Street to transform into the party of your dreams, with our main stage landing right near the Rainbow crossing.</p><p>You heard it here, folks. We&rsquo;re shutting down the street, throwing K Road the biggest party you&rsquo;ve ever seen, and bringing you the wildest line-up in the festival&rsquo;s history. You don&rsquo;t wanna miss it.<br><br><strong>PLEASE NOTE:&nbsp;</strong><br><strong>THIS IS AN ALL AGES EVENT, BUT ALL AGES TICKETS DO NOT GRANT ACCESS TO ALL ZONES, ONLY TO DEDICATED ALL AGES STAGES (FLYING OUT BASEMENT + PITT ST METHODIST CHURCH)</strong><br><br><strong>UNDER 15s MUST BE ACCOMPANIED BY A PARENT OR LEGAL GUARDIAN</strong></p>	1036701081	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1036701081?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:24:01	2025-10-24 12:36:33	{droppER}	10658	t
