4590357	2026-01-24 19:30:00	With the release of their new album Welcome to My Blue Sky (April 2025), Momma cemented their place as one of the most exciting voices in indie rock and now they announce their debut Australian tour for January 2026, making stops in Sydney, Brisbane, and Melbourne.<br><br>We are so excited to be hitting Australia next year! We’ve been looking forward to playing this country for so long, can’t wait to see all of you &lt;333 - Momma<br><br>Like so many coming-of-age stories that leave a long-lasting impact, Momma’s new album Welcome to My Blue Sky takes place during a charmed and turbulent summer — a transformative moment in time that co-founders Etta Friedman and Allegra Weingarten sum up as a period of “parallel chaos.” The result is a bold leap forward for one of the most creatively uncompromising and distinctive talents in indie rock.<br><br>Welcome to My Blue Sky marks the follow-up to Household Name, Momma’s critically acclaimed 2022 release that solidified their rise. Praised by outlets like Rolling Stone, Pitchfork, Stereogum, Paste, NYLON, and The FADER, and building momentum through tours with Alex G, beabadoobee, Wet Leg, as well as appearances at Coachella and Primavera Sound, the band’s ascent shows no signs of slowing. Momma are currently on tour across the US, UK, and Europe, playing their biggest venues to date.<br><br>Joining Momma on their first Australian tour is Melbourne band Armlock. On their new album, Seashell Angel Lucky Charm, the duo take you through a steady ascension into heavenly sonic realms, making the ear candy choruses on tracks like ‘Fear’ and ‘El Oh Vee Ee', which feel like expertly placed moments of guitar pop bliss.<br>Important Event Information: https://www.frontiertouring.com/page/terms-of-sale	1036420792	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1036420792?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:28:20	2025-10-24 12:36:55	{Momma,Armlock}	9466	t
