4592883	2025-11-27 19:00:00	Join us for An Evening With,  a special night of music, stories, and connection featuring The Joy Formidable alongside the solo projects of its founding members, Shy Western (Ritzy Bryan) and Rhydian Dafydd.\nShy Western brings an intimate, pulse-driven energy with nature at its core.\nRhydian Dafydd explores the shadow and the self through a visionarium of driving, folding rhythms, rich textures, and emotional depth.\nWith songs spanning 15 years, exclusive music club tracks, and the occasional surprise guest, An Evening With is a night built on beauty, connection, and offers fans a rare chance to experience these artists up close, in their most open and creative form.	107481241	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107481241?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:33:23	2025-10-24 12:37:29	{"The Joy Formidable"}	6451	t
4592893	2025-11-29 11:00:00	Rolling Sets Doubles Up: Two Beachfront Locations, One Massive Festival with Hilltop Hoods, Spacey Jane, Parcels and More\n\nRolling Sets has cemented itself as a summer staple, selling out every edition since launching on the Central Coast. Its waterfront home at Memorial Park, The Entrance, has played host to massive crowds and unforgettable sets and in 2025, the festival levels up again, expanding into brand new territory with a second location in Tweed Heads. With two coastal throwdowns now on the calendar, this year promises to be Rolling Sets’ biggest yet - rolling into two epic beachfront locations for 2025.\n\nIn this major expansion, the much-loved festival is heading north, taking over Ebenezer Park - Duranbah Beach (Dbah) on Saturday 29 November, then on Saturday 6 December, returning to Memorial Park, The Entrance for the Central Coast edition.\n\nA convergence of live music, surf and skate culture, Rolling Sets brings the energy of a major city festival with the vibes of cruisy coastal living, with this year’s lineup packing serious heat.\n\nTopping the 2025 bill; Hilltop Hoods are returning to the RS stage after launching the Central Coast edition back in 2022. With a brand new album ‘Fall From The Light’ , taking out the coveted Number 2 spot in triple j’s Hottest 100 of Australian Songs, as well as two other entries and a close to sold out national tour under the belt, the band's trajectory is far from slowing down.\n\nRounding out the lineup are Indie darlings Spacey Jane,  electro-funk outfit Parcels (Tweed exclusive), festival faves The Jungle Giants, punk-psych icons Skegss (Central Coast exclusive), and rising US alt-rockers Flipturn (USA). They’re joined by one of the country’s most explosive hardcore acts Speed, alt-pop powerhouse MAY-A, The Terrys, DICE, Blusher, 3%, Scowl (USA) and so many more.\n\nThis year Rolling Sets are partnering with Humanitix as the official ticket seller. Their ticketing platform that takes the booking fees we all hate paying and dedicates the profits to charity. With a focus on helping the world’s most disadvantaged children, 100% of Humanitix’s profits go to charities providing education, healthcare and life’s basic necessities.\n\nRolling Sets x Spirited Foundation - Paddle Out for Hope\n\nThis year, Rolling Sets Festival proudly partners with Spirited Foundation for the World’s Largest Ever Paddle Out, happening on Saturday 6th December 2025 during our Central Coast edition. Spirited Foundation is dedicated to empowering young people impacted by domestic violence through resilience, leadership, and community programs. The global paddle out honours the ocean’s power to inspire healing and connection. Join us, donate onsite, and be part of a global movement supporting youth in need. For more information or to sign up please visit spirited.org.au	107226338	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107226338?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:33:24	2025-10-24 12:37:29	{"The Jungle Giants"}	8148	t
