rial.  In the midst, Blunstone still managed to record three solo releases - The Ghost Of You And Me in 2009, On The Air Tonight in 2012 and most recently, the EP Less is More in early 2024, a set of 5 sparsely-recorded demos showcasing those velvety vocals accompanied only by acoustic guitar.\n \nBlunstone celebrated his 80th birthday in June at the London premiere of Hung Up On A Dream: The Zombies Documentary, the first-ever feature film chronicling the band’s journey from teenage friends to Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Inductees (now available on AppleTV and Amazon).  \n \nWith Argent’s retirement for health reasons in 2024, Blunstone is refocusing on his solo career while also continuing to celebrate the legacy of The Zombies.  A new album is planned for release in 2026.\n\nwww.colinblunstone.net\n	107422028	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107422028?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:34:52	2025-10-24 12:37:36	{"The Zombies","Colin Blunstone"}	7021	t
