4591218	2025-10-25 12:00:00	4ZZZ - ZED50\nA Market Day celebration of 50 years of 4ZZZ radio.\nCelebrating 50 years of people powered radio \n\nBrisbane’s iconic 4ZZZFM underground radio – 50 years of activated media uniqueness... a gravitational mass of marginalised minds blazing with subcultural creativity and political criticality. From the mayhem of those wild market days through to the transmitted waves of boundless idiosyncratic character - enormous in presence and profound in essence. Come celebrate half a century of vital radio and the culture that emanates at ZED50 - Saturday 25 October at Roma St Parklands - a core event as part of 4ZZZ 50th anniversary.\n\nAfter much deliberation, a line-up assembled into collective agreement with the top lining historical tandem of Briz rock pioneers international break out sensations THE SAINTS ’73-'78 - back for another grand blast after their sold-out Princess shows late ‘24. We know our product! \n\nFeaturing a local swag of richness with a smattering of interstate… Brisbane’s genre crunchers REGURGITATOR; warp minding trash pop experimenters TROPICAL FUCK STORM; the driving tempo thunder of high rising FULL FLOWER MOON BAND; the raging politic of Brigg's hot off the press powered-up BIG NOTER; the punk funked gristle and hamming it up of BUTTERFINGERS; the raw impatient scorch and melody of the long lived SCREAMFEEDER; the crunchy, swirling, psych poppin’ colour of NICE BISCUIT; the jazz butchered mayhem of the dynamo duo that is PARTY DOZEN; the neo-soul punk activism of first nations DANCINGWATER; the endearing fuck-you top of the hundred, fruity punk of FLANGIPANIS; the out of the window, queer as folk, rock pulp of PLATONIC SEX; and the many minds that make rock future light work of VELOCIRAPTOR.\n\nTwo stages of market day mania. C'mon Brisbane, you got clout... let's rise to what 4ZZZ community radio is, was, and will be... and a make full day at the parklands of it! \n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/ZED50   \nhttps://www.instagram.com/zedfifty/	106995214	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/106995214?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:30:01	2025-10-24 12:37:06	{Regurgitator,"Tropical Fuck Storm",Butterfingers,Screamfeeder,Velociraptor,Flangipanis,"Full Flower Moon Band","Party Dozen","Nice Biscuit","Platonic Sex","The Saints '73-'78"}	8201	t
4591351	2025-11-25 20:00:00	Doors: 8PM / Show: 9PM / 21+SantahLast time we saw Santah, they were floating down the Chicago river and into Lake Michigan for what was supposed to be their final farewell show. Now, 10 years after their last offering, Santah returns with LAST WHIRLPOOL, the full-length record landing in late 2025.Recorded over a long weekend in the summer of 2024, the kinetic collection of new songs captures the band feeling loose and feeling themselves. Messy and honest, the album tells the (true) tale of extraterrestrials who land on Earth and learn that love hurts. Blissfully unequipped for all of the pleasure and pain on their newfound Neverland, they are eager to taste it all. So they learn how to do the dance, love recklessly, and fall for human touch again and again.On LAST WHIRLPOOL, Santah dives in headfirst and unabashedly embraces the weird romance of it all, delivering some real emotional bangers and shiny barnburners in the process.Before playing their last show in 2017, Santah spent much of the decade prior touring the country and sharing their dreamy indie rock from releases like WHITE NOISE BED (2010), YOURE STILL A LOVER (2012), and CHICO (2015). Theyve since stayed lifelong friends, have sang in each others weddings, and have continued creating music via many different avenues (like V.V. Lightbody, The Curls, Valebol, Lake Soda, BAUGS, Fernando House, Morning Hues, and Family of Geniuses).This November, Santah will come together for a few special shows to celebrate bringing LAST WHIRLPOOL to life.MarrowA four-piece band hailing from Chicago, IL. Marrow is Macie Stewart, Liam Kazar, Dorian Gehring and Matt Carroll. Their last show was 430 weeks ago and they will be performing this evening as a duo (Liam & Macie).	1036242003	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1036242003?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:30:22	2025-10-24 12:37:08	{Santah}	9137	t
