4591607	2025-10-31 19:00:00	Crash Into Earth is an interstellar-themed, UFO crash site, All ages Halloween music festival set in Costa Mesa, CA at the Orange County Fair and Event Center. Through the eyes of two aliens crash-landing on Earth, victims of 5G interference, orbiting satellites, space trash and radioactive chaos, this event reimagines our world as a strange and wondrous party worth crashing. As their ship trembles and systems fail, one alien panics:\n“Are we going to crash into Earth?”\nThe other, trying to make sense of the readouts, stares down through the clouds and spots a glowing sign: “Crash Into Earth”and they realize they’re not doomed… they’re invited.\n“Yes… We are definitely going to crash into Earth!!!!!!!! And it's going to be sick!!!”\nWith performances by  Allah-Las, Babe Rainbow, Skegss, Discovery Zone, Yasawa Group, Will Worden, Seventies Tuberide, Monde UFO, Big Fun, Sepe, Soft Palms, Buddy Crime, Neo Globs, Mel Gibson, Plus EDM and Techno from the  "Bounce House,"  this cosmic convergence features two stages, carnival rides, rollerskating on the moon, and barn-side crop circle dance zones, Costume contest with $500 reward and surfboard raffle. It’s part invasion, part celebration - a place where Earth meets the outer limits littered with UFO crash sites. It’s not a disaster. It’s destiny.\nThis October, COME MAKE CONTACT!	107313389	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107313389?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:30:56	2025-10-24 12:37:12	{"Soft Palms",Allah-Las,"The Babe Rainbow",Skeggs,"Will Worden","Discovery Zone","YASAWA GROUP","Big Fun","Monde UFO",Sepe,"Buddy Crime","NEO GLOBS","Mel Gibson"}	10501	t
4591448	2026-02-03 20:00:00	Tickets at www.LaRosaTucson.com----Best Life PresentsshameTuesday, November 3rd 16+Standing room onlyVeranda Bar opens at 6:30pmVenue doors open at 7:15pmShow starts at 8pm***VIDEO***Following in the footsteps of unflinching musicians and writers such as the Fall, Television Personalities, and Irvine Welsh, South Londons bracing post-punk outfit Shame features vocalist Charlie Steen, guitarists Sean Coyle-Smith and Eddie Green, bassist Josh Finerty, and drummer Charlie Forbes. The quintet met in school and formed Shame in 2014 while still in their teens. A family connection led them to practice at the Queens Head, a gritty Brixton pub that was also home to Fat White Family. Gigs with that band, the Garden, and Slaves led to an appearance at 2016s Pitchfork Music Festival Paris; later that year, Shame released their debut single The Lick/Gold Hole on Fnord Communications. In 2017, the band signed with Dead Oceans and released the singles Tasteless, Concrete, and Visa Vulture, a commentary on Prime Minister Theresa Mays stance on immigration. That year, Shame recorded their debut album, Songs of Praise, at Wales Rockfield Studios; the album arrived in early 2018.	1035873970	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1035873970?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:30:37	2025-10-24 12:37:09	{Shame}	10173	t
4591425	2025-11-06 20:00:00	REMCA PRÉSENTE : SHAMEShame on tourShame revient plus fort, plus tranchant, plus essentiel que jamais avec Cutthroat, un nouvel album prévu pour 2025, produit par John Congleton (St. Vincent, Angel Olsen). Un disque sans compromis, grandiose et nerveux, où se croisent guitares acérées et boucles électroniques, porté par une énergie brute et indomptable. Premier extrait : une bombe hédoniste et urgente, probablement leur meilleur titre à ce jour. Avec leur post-punk tendu et fiévreux, Shame ausculte l’époque à grands coups de riffs et de sarcasme. Charlie Steen et sa bande n’ont jamais eu la langue dans leur poche : entre introspection, politique et provoc’, leurs concerts sont tout sauf sages – et toujours légendaires. Seulement quatre dates en France pour cette tournée, dont un passage à La Cartonnerie de Reims. Autant dire que c’est à ne pas rater. Post-punk anglais sans filtre et sans paillettes. Préparez-vous à en prendre plein les oreilles.	1035533565	https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1035533565?app_id=51fbb96b1e0a3466197c51b74bc89eac&came_from=267&utm_medium=api&utm_source=public_api&utm_campaign=event	2025-10-24 12:30:36	2025-10-24 12:37:10	{Shame}	10173	t
